    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d970">

                <pb facs="0897" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/7113.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Ambassador.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-04-17T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1913—8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. Your April 12, 2 p.m. The <hi rendition="#italic">Georgia</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Virginia</hi> will be relieved respectively by the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minnesota</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Idaho</hi>,
                    which sailed April 16 from Philadelphia. The <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Connecticut</hi> will sail about April 22 to relieve the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Vermont</hi>. These changes should remove the danger of
                    embarrassment pointed out by Mr. de la Barra. You will inform the authorities
                    and request that the usual courtesies be accorded the new vessels on
                    arrival.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
